    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50868" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victōrĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		victoria, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to victory</i>
			(late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: dies, <i>day of
			victory</i>, i. e. <i>when victories are
			celebrated</i>, Treb. Gall. 3: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scipio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 6, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victōrĭālis</span></b> ,
			is, f., <i>a plant</i>, <i>called also</i> Idaea Daphne,
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 58</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Isid. 10, 210</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
